    "blurb": "Quantum circuits inside BPMN workflows",
    "overview": "Execute quantum circuits on real IBM Quantum hardware directly from your Camunda 8 BPMN workflows. It supports Sampler and Estimator primitives, blocking and polling execution modes, and OpenQASM circuit input.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Connect your BPMN processes to real IBM Quantum hardware",
    "splashDescription": "Quantum computing offers powerful capabilities for optimization, simulation, and sampling problems that classical hardware cannot efficiently solve — but integrating it into enterprise workflows has historically required specialized tooling outside the reach of most process engineers. The IBM Quantum Connector makes quantum execution a native step in any Camunda 8 BPMN process, submitting circuits to real IBM Quantum hardware via the Qiskit Runtime REST API. It supports Sampler and Estimator primitives, OpenQASM circuit input, and both blocking and polling execution modes to accommodate the variable queue times of live quantum hardware. Results are returned as structured process variables, ready for use in any downstream step.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/808030/overview/img6717189578193572307.png?fd5a9db805c642235e80b8c8524f9f56",
